[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I think so.

01:14:10.934 --> 01:14:12.114
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, very much.

01:14:13.315 --> 01:14:18.878
[SPEAKER_00]: I think during Buddha's time, many of the kings were kings, but still the benefactor of Buddha.

01:14:19.879 --> 01:14:21.500
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not like that.

01:14:22.140 --> 01:14:23.701
[SPEAKER_00]: Once Lama Shon was in Bhutan,

01:14:24.673 --> 01:14:26.374
[SPEAKER_00]: And he went to a vegetable market.

01:14:28.335 --> 01:14:34.018
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the vegetable seller, they're selling, what was it?

01:14:34.419 --> 01:14:35.079
[SPEAKER_00]: Asparagus.

01:14:35.899 --> 01:14:40.262
[SPEAKER_00]: So he says, he spoke in Tibetan, ,, which means how much it is.

01:14:41.022 --> 01:14:44.584
[SPEAKER_00]: And because his Tibetan is so good, she didn't realize he was a white man.

01:14:45.645 --> 01:14:47.666
[SPEAKER_00]: So she said, 20 rupees.

01:14:47.706 --> 01:14:49.067
[SPEAKER_00]: And she looked up and said, 50.

01:14:54.622 --> 01:14:56.404
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's not so good.

01:15:06.772 --> 01:15:19.082
[SPEAKER_00]: So you can be an honest, reasonable businessman, then you're doing business to gain some kind of benefit or living.

01:15:20.738 --> 01:15:28.423
[SPEAKER_00]: And also, there's, of course, one special about Buddhism is that the intention is very important.

01:15:29.403 --> 01:15:39.749
[SPEAKER_00]: So even when you do business, you can have, do some, accumulate some, how do you say, worldly means, so eventually I will be able to practice Dharma.

01:15:40.690 --> 01:15:41.850
[SPEAKER_00]: Then it's also good, you know.

01:15:42.231 --> 01:15:44.372
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think very much intention.

01:15:45.453 --> 01:15:47.634
[SPEAKER_00]: And I sometimes say,

01:15:49.895 --> 01:15:50.819
[SPEAKER_00]: switching off light.

01:15:51.823 --> 01:15:54.352
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just the same action, you switch off light.

01:15:56.472 --> 01:16:21.629
[SPEAKER_00]: just switch off light in order to save your electricity bill then it's switching off light but it's selfish switch off the light is to save the environment same time you save electricity bill that's little bit greater view save electricity bill for the sake of all sentient beings then bodhisattva electricity

01:16:23.110 --> 01:16:25.092
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think it very much depends on intention.

01:16:25.952 --> 01:16:39.902
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why I think in Buddhism, mostly I think we have to check our intention in everything we do, even practice, even meditation.

01:16:40.923 --> 01:16:49.529
[SPEAKER_00]: If we can add the attitude of meditation for the sake of all sentient beings, then it becomes Mahayana, Vajrayana meditation.

01:16:50.476 --> 01:17:15.387
[SPEAKER_00]: or meditation, even that, what was it, that fashionable one, mindfulness, even a mindfulness, fashionable one, even the mindfulness, for the sake of all sentient beings, I think it can be, you know, as a Buddhist practice, mindfulness so that I can become a smarter businessman, it's selfish, so it very much depends on our intention.

01:17:16.983 --> 01:17:17.163
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

01:17:17.983 --> 01:17:25.366
[SPEAKER_00]: Rinpoche, there was a follow-up question on the last one, which was, what did Lama Shawn say to the 50 rupees?

01:17:28.827 --> 01:17:30.208
[SPEAKER_00]: Did you give 50 or 20?

01:17:31.288 --> 01:17:34.129
[SPEAKER_00]: I went to the next woman.

01:17:38.891 --> 01:17:40.511
[SPEAKER_00]: OK, that's a skillful means.

01:17:48.196 --> 01:17:59.685
[SPEAKER_00]: There are a few questions that seem related, which is how to mix the view that you've presented tonight of recognizing the nature of mind with everyday life.

01:18:00.726 --> 01:18:02.368
[SPEAKER_00]: So for example, relationships.

01:18:03.789 --> 01:18:08.172
[SPEAKER_00]: For example, working with other types of sadhana practices that have ritual and form.

01:18:08.973 --> 01:18:09.854
[SPEAKER_00]: How do you mix the view?

01:18:15.637 --> 01:18:15.958
[SPEAKER_00]: OK.

01:18:16.959 --> 01:18:18.562
[SPEAKER_00]: So I will answer the second question.

01:18:18.582 --> 01:18:19.643
[SPEAKER_00]: It is easier, first.

01:18:21.807 --> 01:18:30.280
[SPEAKER_00]: So, any practice sadhana we do, it has, ultimately, at the end, the accomplishment stage.

01:18:31.935 --> 01:18:47.726
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think every practice, different layers or different levels, but somehow there is always shamatha and vipassana, shine and lakthong, development and completion stage.

01:18:54.351 --> 01:19:20.341
[SPEAKER_00]: the sadhana practice we do all these visualizations deities whatever the mantra garlands and all this and then everything dissolved and then rest into the nature of mind so i think there's always at the end of the any sadhana any practice resting a natural mind so i don't think it really contradicts

01:19:22.523 --> 01:19:37.128
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, I think the most important, I think if you receive the proper instruction and guidance, then I think it's important to work with your mind, trying to rest in the nature of mind.

01:19:38.608 --> 01:19:44.410
[SPEAKER_00]: And I don't know whether I'll be able to answer the first question clearly or not, but I think

01:19:45.160 --> 01:19:57.614
[SPEAKER_00]: then naturally, when you have some kind of understanding or some experience of the nature of mind, your negative emotions might naturally reduce.

01:19:59.567 --> 01:20:10.397
[SPEAKER_00]: And then when there's less negative emotions, I think there's less to argue or fight among the couples.

01:20:12.038 --> 01:20:13.079
[SPEAKER_00]: That was the question, right?

01:20:13.220 --> 01:20:14.381
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, about relationships.

01:20:14.401 --> 01:20:15.301
[SPEAKER_00]: About relationships.

01:20:17.604 --> 01:20:21.187
[SPEAKER_00]: Then maybe a good opportunity to meditate on patience also.

01:20:23.583 --> 01:20:24.764
[SPEAKER_00]: or understanding, right?

01:20:26.225 --> 01:20:42.315
[SPEAKER_00]: Also, Patrul Rinpoche's story, one time that one man is sort of meditating in the hermitage, and Patrul Rinpoche asked him, What are you meditating on?

01:20:42.555 --> 01:20:45.277
[SPEAKER_00]: He said, Oh, I'm meditating on Zobah, patience.

01:20:46.797 --> 01:20:51.421
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he whispered in his ear, people like you and me can fool people these days.

01:20:51.862 --> 01:20:54.344
[SPEAKER_00]: And he got so angry, why are you coming here and bothering me?

01:21:01.711 --> 01:21:11.460
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think, as a practitioner, as a Buddhist, as a practitioner, when things go well,

01:21:12.575 --> 01:21:20.800
[SPEAKER_00]: then we don't really know how good our practice is or how much depth there is when in practice.

01:21:20.980 --> 01:21:25.022
[SPEAKER_00]: So when circumstances arise, that's the time I think we have to use.

01:21:26.503 --> 01:21:36.209
[SPEAKER_00]: So sometimes I think if you want to see some of how deep or how good you are, then some challenge maybe.

01:21:39.509 --> 01:21:42.490
[SPEAKER_00]: something that will stir up your negative emotions.

01:21:42.970 --> 01:21:45.631
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you can see whether you can handle it or not.

01:21:46.591 --> 01:21:51.853
[SPEAKER_00]: And some of the lojong practice, lojong teaching, it's almost like you have to look for trouble.

01:21:53.247 --> 01:21:53.868
[SPEAKER_00]: Almost like that.

01:21:53.908 --> 01:22:01.696
[SPEAKER_00]: Not really you poke on somebody, but you almost look for trouble, and you're fully ready to challenge any problem.

01:22:02.176 --> 01:22:09.024
[SPEAKER_00]: So when the problem arises, you say, OK, now I can use my lojong tactics.

01:22:12.054 --> 01:22:17.158
[SPEAKER_00]: against the negative emotions.

01:22:17.698 --> 01:22:22.642
[SPEAKER_00]: So this is the main purpose of practice, becoming a better practitioner.

01:22:23.062 --> 01:22:31.128
[SPEAKER_00]: I have many friends, Westerners, Easterners, disciples of Khyentse Rinpoche, many.

01:22:32.129 --> 01:22:37.573
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't really see them levitating or having a hollow on their head.

01:22:38.402 --> 01:22:43.884
[SPEAKER_00]: But I've seen them becoming a better human being, less attached to the worldly life.

01:22:47.686 --> 01:22:49.327
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think that's the result of the practice.

01:22:50.247 --> 01:22:59.631
[SPEAKER_00]: So I think the problem is, if you can look at it as a challenge, being a Buddhist practitioner, not much fear.

01:23:00.651 --> 01:23:07.214
[SPEAKER_00]: And of course, being most important, not much hope and fear.

01:23:10.720 --> 01:23:16.287
[SPEAKER_00]: Rinpoche, thank you so much for sharing the Dharma with us tonight.

